another topic that loomis got into  and we have the stories at pft with the  full quotes i'm not going to read  anything verbatim in part because i  don't have it in front of me but mickey  loom has talked about the two main  candidates to become quarterback of the  team this year starter who will it be  will it be taysom hill will it be jameis  winston winston became a free agent  after the 2020 season he signed a deal  that pays him less than what taysom hill  is due to make this year i don't know  that that really matters here's what i  go back to  in 2020 when drew brees got injured  remember he had i think more broken ribs  than there are ribs in the human body  but when brees got injured  and we spent a whole week  thinking  based on reporting that was being done  at the time that jameis winston would be  the starter and then all of a sudden  we find out friday of  the week in advance of i think it was a  game against the falcons  that taysom hill would get the nod  what sean payton eventually said  at that time in that general  period  was that he had given his word to taysom  hill  that if brees got injured during the  2020 season hill would get the  opportunity to replace him he had made  that promise to taysom hill because the  year before obviously it was teddy  bridgewater who went 5-0  while drew brees was injured he had that  thumb injury that he suffered against  the rams i believe it was so  last year  hill  had been given that promise and remember  hill  signed a new contract in the offseason  was going to be a restricted free agent  had to decide to stay with the saints  reup with the saints  and i think part of that conversation  was  as  peyton told the world he'd given  hill his word that he'd get the chance  if brees got injured but at that same  time  peyton also said  he'd promised jameis winston he'll have  a chance to compete for the starting job  in 2021 now that was kind of odd at the  time because winston's only under  contract through 2020 but it it made it  clear that the saints wanted to bring  winston back winston became a free agent  no one flocked to try to sign him to the  kind of contract that would make him a  clear-cut starter like the panthers did  with teddy bridgewater in 2020  so winston returns and i think that he's  been promised multiple times now he gets  a chance he gets a chance to compete and  we'll find out who the better option is  now if you go with winston you still  have the taysom hill package that's an  attraction that actually hurts hill the  fact that he can do all those other  things about which loomis rave to adam  shine hurts him in the competition to be  the starter because hey if it's about  putting your best 11 on the field let  winston play quarterback let taysom hill  be the jack of all trades and do  different things  but however it plays out they're gonna  go with the guy that they think gives  them the best chance to win and  it could be something that's decided on  a week-by-week basis it could be  something that's decided on a drive-by  drive or play-by-play basis but it will  be a fair competition i believe and i  think sean payton will go with the guy  that he thinks deserves to play and it  may not be  a 17-game decision that's made week one  against the green bay packers and the  other factor sims and i have talked  about this on pft live  payton has that proclivity  of coming up with plays anywhere and  everywhere up to and including kickoff  sunday morning breakfast got some new  plays that i came up with here they are  which guy is going to be better suited  to adapting to those plays to  incorporating those plays and performing  them the way that sean payton wants them  to be performed brees could do it  hill's been around to watch it but  winston was too remember how emotional  winston was when brees retired how much  winston learned last year about how to  be a pro  one of the things about being a pro is  being flexible and adaptable you never  know what's going to get thrown at you  you have to just keep going  you just keep going no matter what the  potential distraction may be no matter  what the challenge may be and one of the  biggest challenges of playing  quarterback for sean payton  being ready on sunday morning to find  out that the game plan has been expanded  by several more plays  it'd be fun to watch because look bottom  line is  saints continue to be a contender  in the nfc this is nothing against drew  brees our new nbc colleague but  it's no secret the arm strength wasn't  what it used to be later in his career  with hill and winston the arm strength  is there  and  the farther down the field that the  quarterback can throw the ball  the more of the field that the defense  has to defend  it's a testament  to how good drew brees is at diagnosing  and executing the plays that are called  in obvious partnership with sean payton  that that offense can operate at a very  high level even though the defense  doesn't feel compelled  to cover all the way to the goal line  now this year you add in the reality  that  if you creep up to the line of scrimmage  someone may run right by you and that  ball is going to go over the top and  it's not going to be  underthrown it's going to land right in  the hands of the wide open receiver  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports
 

